From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: The MP3 encoder MFT (9404)

Wine had no MP3 encoder MFT (CLSID_MP3ACMCodecWrapper, Windows 8 and later): NAudio's
MediaFoundationEncoder.EncodeToMp3 and sink writers to .mp3 found none. As documented ("MP3 Audio
Encoder"): output type first, MPEG-1 layer 3 at 32/44.1/48 kHz and 32-320 kbps, the
MPEGLAYER3WAVEFORMAT tail in MF_MT_USER_DATA, one frame per output sample; through wg_transform
(GStreamer's LAME encoder, asked for a constant bit rate in kbit/s). Registered by winegstreamer
itself (the Windows DLL holding it is not documented).
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/mp3_encoder.c
@@ -0,0 +1,771 @@
